hey folks Chris waters here standing in  for reviewer Justin Clark some of your  greatest moments in Kerbal space program  are likely to be failures you endured  disaster after disaster keeping the  little green men that inhabit this  universe alive in the cold blackness of  space and then their ship crashes into  the moon which means the end for them  but it also means triumph for you  their commander you finally made it  after all that time spent trying and  tweaking and now it's time to try again  and hopefully to stick the landing this  time trying to nutshell Kerbal space  program isn't so much a matter of  straightforward you win if you get here  goals the game never stops because  there's an entire solar system waiting  out there to be explored what the game  values above all else is perseverance  you advance by simply having the  boldness to reach a little higher if you  manage to break the world speed record  then you're ready to try reaching the  upper atmosphere if you can get there  then maybe we can put an astronaut in  space and if we can reach space maybe we  can reach our closest planetary neighbor  most of your time and game is spent in  the Vehicle Assembly Building on  constant trial-and-error mode trying to  build a craft that can do exactly what's  required for the mission at hand there  are literally hundreds of design options  and moving parts to assemble from fuel  tanks and rockets to the heat shields  for re-entry and the decoupling devices  for boosters and you'd better take it  all into consideration or your vessel  will crash and burn before you even see  the Stars the actual crafting process is  dirt simple where every part is attached  to your craft like Legos there's a slew  of fine tuning tools available for the  more meticulous player but it's a long  time before they become necessary evils  during the design process you have to  plan for every stage of the mission you  need to stockpile enough fuel to make it  there and back and you've always got to  keep in mind your ships stability  and once you've got your spacecraft the  real struggle begins and your real  opponent is gravity gravity is what  keeps craft from lifting off because  you've got too much fuel or not enough  boosters and it's what you will fight  all the way into the upper atmosphere  trying to put spacecrafts in orbit  instead of watching them fall helplessly  back to the ground there are three  different modes in Kerbal space program  sandbox mode opens up every available  part in the game for you to just fool  around with the most elaborate and  insane designs imaginable in science  mode you earn points for every new  milestone you achieve and then spend  them on the research and development  skill tree which is where you earn  bigger and better parts to use career  mode is a full-blown space program  experience where money is an object and  public donations and government  contracts are required to even afford to  send astronauts on a flight this mode is  the most gamey of them all with  contracts representing clearly defined  missions you can perform to get the most  out of every flight Kerbal space program  was in beta for years before this its  official release funny enough even after  all that time there are still some  scattered bugs throughout like ships  occasionally disappearing and orbital  paths turning twitchy and changing at  random even while your ship follows the  one you set but these are nitpicks  compared to what feels like the  cumulative achievements of thousands of  minds bringing their expertise to the  table you see it in the hundreds of  tweaks done over the years and in the  lovingly crafted mods which are easily  accessible and promoted in game even  nasa's gotten in on it with a few of  their own hypothetical scenarios  pre-loaded in the game right from the  get-go you will fail at Kerbal space  program but you will eventually find  success it will demoralize you it will  stress you out but more often than not  it will also soothe you and inspire you  every failure has a lesson to impart and  every lesson brings you closer to a new  accomplishment successes in Kerbal space  program may be hard earned but they're  all the sweeter for it whether you're  escaping the atmosphere for the very  first time or planting a flag on an  unexplored planet  you
 

